e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "s out as 0 with no warning.\n- `app/config.py` loads the file correctly, so it isn't involved.\n\n**Suggested fix:**\n1. Rename `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"` in `settings.json:2`. That is enough to fix the total.\n2. Optionally, change `main.py:10-13` so it doesn't swallow the `KeyError`. A bad config would then fail with an error instead of printing 0.\n\nDo you want me to apply either change?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: list]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe setting `fee_rate` is read in three places, and all three work now.\n\n**Where it is read**\n- `main.py:11` reads `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`. A `KeyError` is caught and turned into `rate = 0`.\n- `billing/report.py:7` calls `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` and exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if the result is `None`.\n- `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` calls `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`. The key is built by string concatenation, so a plain search for `fee_rate` misses it. It exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" if the result is `None`.\n\n**Other matches that don't read the setting**\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` sets `column = \"fee_rate\"`. That is a historical column-name string, and its docstring says the total doesn't use it.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` sets `archived_fee_rate = 0.15`. That is a hardcoded constant and never touches the config.\n- `billing/csv_writer.py:10` and `billing/report.py:9` only mention `fee_rate` in their error messages.\n\n**Fix:** In `settings.json:2` I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. All three paths read the same file through `app/config.py`, so that one change fixed them all.\n\n**Check:** I ran all three paths after the change:\n- `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0`.\n- `python3 -m billing.report` prints `Report fee: 0.5`.\n- `python3 -m billing.export.csv_writer` prints `CSV fee: 0.5`.\n\nI left the `try/except KeyError` in `main.py` alone. It will still print `Total: 0` instead of failing if the key goes missing again. Say if you want it to fail loudly like the other two.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 9, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 127691, "requests_cache_write": 33596, "requests_cost_usd": 0.13700310000000002, "requests_count": 14, "requests_input_uncached": 1477, "requests_output": 3729, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial13", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 108, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T02:37:50.664680+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 2, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 35.08, "t_checker_s": 0.222, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5206, "tokens_cache_read": 127691, "tokens_cache_write": 33596, "tokens_fresh": 2394, "tokens_input_uncached": 1477, "tokens_main_cache_read": 97864, "tokens_main_cache_write": 20281, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 2376, "tokens_output": 3729, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 127691, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 33596, "tokens_proxy_calls": 14, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1477, "tokens_proxy_output": 3729, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.8", "anthropic": "2.0.0", "bun": "1.3.2"}, "tr